cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use ChessNets, please cite it as below, and also cite the papers
  behind the specific models you use.
type: software
title: "ChessNets: State-of-the-art models for playing chess and human move imitation"
authors:
  - family-names: Siu
    given-names: Sherman
version: 0.1.1
date-released: 2026-11-23
# Concept DOI: always resolves to the latest version.
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24458166
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/shermansiu/chessnets"
abstract: >-
  ChessNets is a PyTorch library that loads Lc0, Maia, Maia 2, UniMaia,
  Allie, ChessGPT, and ChessCLIP checkpoints through one pipeline API, and
  runs them as UCI engines or Lichess bots.
keywords:
  - chess
  - human move prediction
  - neural networks
  - pytorch
